t is 40 minus 15 and 10. Let me compute that.\n\nSo 40 minus 15 is 25. Then 25 minus 10 is 15. Therefore, she had 15kg. Yes, that matches. So maybe my initial answer is correct. Alternatively, maybe I can think of it as 15 + 10 is 25, so 40 - 25 = 15. Therefore, she had 15kg. Yep, same thing. Therefore, the answer should be 15 kg.\n</think>\n\nElise bought a 15kg bag and a 10kg bag. She now has a total of 40kg. To find out how much she already had:\n\n1. Let $ x $ be the amount she had before the trips.\n2. The total dog food she has now is the sum of her initial amount and the new amounts: $ x + 15 + 10 = 40 $.\n3. Solving for $ x $, we get $ x = 40 - 15 - 10 = 15 $.\n\nThus, Elise had $ \\boxed{15} $ kg of dog food.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Elise is buying more dog food. She buys a 15kg bag then another 10kg bag, and she now has 40kg of dog food. How many kilograms of dog food did Elise already have?", "answer": "Elise has bought a total of 15 kg + 10 kg = <<15+10=25>>25kg of dog food.\nThis means she already had 40 kg – 25 kg = <<40-25=15>>15kg of dog food.\n#### 15", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Elise is buying more dog food. She buys a 15kg bag then another 10kg bag, and she now has 40kg of dog food. How many kilograms of dog food did Elise already have?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["15"], "solution": "15"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 3984, 1064, 374, 11833, 803, 5562, 3607, 13, 2932, 49531, 264, 220, 16, 20, 7351, 8968, 1221, 2441, 220, 16, 15, 7351, 8968, 11, 323, 1340, 1431, 702, 220, 19, 15, 7351, 315, 5562, 3607, 13, 2585], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 3984, 1064, 374, 11833, 803, 5562, 3607, 13, 2932, 49531, 264, 220, 16, 20, 7351, 8968, 323, 2441, 220, 16, 15, 7