t let me double-check. Total is 28. Week 1: 12. Week 2: 1/4 of 12 is 3. Total painted in both weeks is 12 + 3 = 15. 28 - 15 = 13. So the answer is 13. So written in boxed notation, \\boxed{13}. Let me just check again. 1/4 of 12 is 3. Yes. 12 + 3 = 15. 28 - 15 = 13. Alright. I think that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{13}\n</think>\n\nMichelangelo has a total of 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he paints $ \\frac{1}{4} $ of the number of ceilings he painted this week. This week, he paints 12 ceilings.\n\n- February: 12 ceilings painted\n- Next week: $ \\frac{1}{4} \\times 12 = 3 $ ceilings painted\n\nAfter both weeks, the number of ceilings painted is $ 12 + 3 = 15 $. The total number of ceilings is 28, so the number of ceilings left to paint is:\n\n$$\n28 - 15 = \\boxed{13}\n$$\n\nThus, the answer is $\\boxed{13}$.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?", "answer": "After this week, Michelangelo will have 28-12=<<28-12=16>>16 more ceilings to paint.\nNext week, Michelangelo will paint 12/4=<<12/4=3>>3 ceilings.\nMichelangelo will have 16-3=<<16-3=13>>13 more ceilings to paint.\n#### 13", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["13"], "solution": "13"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 