ers are there if there are 18 members in the club?", "answer": "The club has a female group which has twice as many members as the male group, so there are 2+1=<<2+1=3>>3 groups in the club.\nThere are 18 members in the club, which means there are 18/3 = <<18/3=6>>6 members per group.\nSince the number of female members consists of two groups, then there are 6 * 2 = <<6*2=12>>12 female members in the club.\n#### 12", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: In a glee club, there are two times as many female than male members. How many female members are there if there are 18 members in the club?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["12"], "solution": "12"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 758, 264, 342, 8501, 6335, 11, 1052, 525, 1378, 3039, 438, 1657, 8778, 1091, 8593, 3613, 13, 2585, 1657, 8778, 3613, 525, 1052, 421, 1052, 525, 220, 16, 23, 3613, 304, 279, 6335, 5267, 36842, 25, 151645], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 13, 2055, 11, 279, 3405, 374, 25, 758, 264, 342, 8501, 6335, 11, 1052, 525, 1378, 3039, 438, 1657, 8778, 1091, 8593, 3613, 13, 2585, 1657, 8778, 3613, 525, 1052, 421, 1052, 525, 220, 16, 23, 3613, 304, 279, 6335, 1939, 80022, 11, 1077, 594, 1438, 419, 1495, 13, 576, 3491, 2727]}
